      "feedback": "静态检查或接口契约失败：\n第 10 行 [E_BAD_CHAR] 无法识别的字符 '{'\n第 10 行 [E_BAD_CHAR] 无法识别的字符 '}'\n第 14 行 [E_BAD_CHAR] 无法识别的字符 '{'\n第 14 行 [E_BAD_CHAR] 无法识别的字符 '}'\n第 18 行 [E_BAD_CHAR] 无法识别的字符 '{'\nLTL 检查：not_run。",
      "idx": 0,
      "code": "I'll implement a Function Block for calculating a moving average in Structured Text. Let me first check the directory structure, then create the implementation.\n\n**Step 1: Check the workspace structure**\n{\"cmd\":[\"dir /b\"]}\n<newline>\n</newline>\n\nI'll create a complete ST implementation for the moving average function block:\n\n{\"cmd\":[\"Get-Content -Path 'fb_moving_average.st' -Raw\"]}\n<newline>\n</newline>\n\n{\"cmd\":[\"Set-Content -Path 'fb_moving_average.st' -Value @'\\nFUNCTION_BLOCK FB_MovingAverage\\nVAR_INPUT\\n    cyclicExecution : BOOL;\\n    trigger : BOOL;\\n    value : LREAL;\\n    windowSize : INT;\\n    reset : BOOL;\\nEND_VAR\\n\\nVAR_OUTPUT\\n    average : LREAL;\\n    windowSizeReached : BOOL;\\n    error : BOOL;\\n    status : WORD;\\nEND_VAR\\n\\nVAR\\n    buffer : ARRAY[1..100] OF LREAL;\\n    index : INT := 1;\\n    count : INT := 0;\\n    sum : LREAL := 0.0;\\n    lastTrigger : BOOL := FALSE;\\n    i : INT;\\nEND_VAR\\n\\n// Main logic\\nIF reset THEN\\n    // Reset all internal state\\n    index := 1;\\n    count := 0;\\n    sum := 0.0;\\n    average := 0.0;\\n    windowSizeReached := FALSE;\\n    error := FALSE;\\n    status := 16#0000;\\n    \\n    // Clear the buffer\\n    FOR i := 1 TO 100 DO\\n        buffer[i] := 0.0;\\n    END_FOR;\\n    \\n    lastTrigger := FALSE;\\n    \\nELSIF windowSize < 1 OR windowSize > 100 THEN\\n    // Window size validation error\\n    error := TRUE;\\n    status := 16#8200;\\n    windowSizeReached := FALSE;\\n    \\nELSE\\n    // Check for update condition: cyclic execution OR rising edge of trigger\\n    IF cyclicExecution OR (trigger AND NOT lastTrigger) THEN\\n        // If buffer is full, subtract the oldest value from sum\\n        // If buffer not full, just increment count\\n        IF count >= windowSize THEN\\n            sum := sum - buffer[index];\\n        ELSE\\n            count := count + 1;\\n        END_IF;\\n        \\n        // Store new value and update sum\\n        buffer[index] := value;\\n        sum := sum + value;\\n        \\n        // Calculate average\\n        average := sum / LREAL_TO_INT(count);\\n        \\n        // Update circular buffer index (wrap around)\\n        index := (index MOD windowSize) + 1;\\n        \\n        // Update windowSizeReached flag\\n        windowSizeReached := (count >= windowSize);\\n        \\n        // Clear error status on successful execution\\n        error := FALSE;\\n        status := 16#0000;\\n    END_IF;\\n    \\n    // Store trigger state for next cycle (rising edge detection)\\n    lastTrigger := trigger;\\nEND_IF;\\n\\nEND_FUNCTION_BLOCK\\n'@\"]}\n<newline>\n</newline>\n\n{\"cmd\":[\"Get-Content -Path 'fb_moving_average.st'\"]}\n<newline>\n</newline>\n\nThe moving average function block has been created at `fb_moving_average.st`.\n\n**Implementation Overview:**\n\n- **Buffer Management:** Uses a circular buffer (array[1..100]) to store values, with index tracking for efficient insertion\n- **Rising Edge Detection:** Stores `lastTrigger` state to detect rising edges on the `trigger` input\n- **Cyclic Execution:** When `cyclicExecution` is TRUE, updates occur every scan cycle regardless of trigger\n- **Window Size Validation:** Checks if windowSize is between 1-100; otherwise sets error status to 16#8200\n- **Reset Function:** Clears buffer, resets all accumulators and state variables\n- **Moving Average Calculation:** Divides sum by current count (not windowSize) until window is full, then divides by windowSize\n\n**Status Codes:**\n- `16#0000`: Successful execution\n- `16#8200`: Window length setting error (outside 1-100 range)\n\n**Usage Example:**\n1. Set `windowSize` to desired buffer length (e.g., 10)\n2. Set `cyclicExecution := TRUE` for automatic updates, or use `trigger` for manual updates\n3. Feed values through `value` input\n4. Read result from `average` output",
